[tool_use] Agent {"description":"Code review of Phase 6.1 implementation","subagent_type":"code-reviewer","prompt":"Review the Phase 6.1 implementation in the pointfight-reactor project at `/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor`. This is the clip library: import, store, list, delete — the first sub-phase of Video Opponent Mode.\n\n**Background:**\n- Phase 6 was decomposed into 6.1/6.2/6.3 with a planning + adversarial review round-trip recorded in `artifacts/decision-memo.md` (`## Phase 6 decomposition memo — Video Opponent Mode` → `### Red-team review` → `### Resolved red-team blockers`).\n- Phase 6.1 acceptance criteria are in `docs/PHASES.md` §\"Phase 6.1: Clip library — import, store, list, delete\".\n- The decision memo §\"Concern 2\", §\"Concern 4\" lock in the exact Dexie v4 declaration and the typed `addClip` return shape; check the implementation matches.\n- Project conventions documented in `docs/QUALITY_GATES.md` and `docs/SPEC.md`.\n- The §B5 concession means real `<video>` duration extraction and live `navigator.storage` behavior are MANUAL-only; pure-logic must be unit-tested.\n\n**Changes in this PR:**\n- New file `app/src/clipmode/types.ts` — ClipRecord, AddClipResult discriminated union, hard/soft size caps, supported MIME types.\n- New file `app/src/clipmode/library.ts` — `addClip`, `listClips`, `deleteClip`, `getQuotaEstimate`, `quotaBanner`, `isSoftWarnSize`.\n- New file `app/src/clipmode/library.test.ts` — 21 tests across the six exports.\n- New file `app/src/ui/ClipLibraryScreen.tsx` — import / list / delete UI; offscreen-`<video>` duration extraction; quota banner; error/soft-warn banners.\n- New file `app/verify-phase6-1.mjs` — Playwright gate checks C1-C4 (Manage clips link, empty state, quota text, close button).\n- Modified `app/src/store/db.ts` — added `clips!: EntityTable<ClipRecord, 'id'>` and `version(4).stores({...})` with the locked-in five-table declaration; `reps` index now includes `clipId`.\n- Modified `app/src/store/db.test.ts` — added two tests in a new `describe('Dexie v3 → v4 upgrade')` block.\n- Modified `app/src/App.tsx` — added `'clips'` to `IdleView`, added `onOpenClips` prop wire-through, route renders `<ClipLibraryScreen>`.\n- Modified `app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx` — added optional `onOpenClips?` prop, renders a `data-testid=\"manage-clips-link\"` button.\n- Modified `app/src/App.css` — added `.clip-library*` styles.\n\n**Verification status:**\n- 213/213 vitest tests pass (190 baseline + 23 new; +2 db, +21 library).\n- Lint, tsc, vite build all clean.\n- Bundle: main 351.57 KB / 108.80 KB gzip (was 345.86 / 107.01). Delta +5.71 raw / +1.79 gzip. Budget was +5 KB gzip → under.\n- `verify-phase6-1.mjs` C1-C4 all PASS, 0 console errors. Results in `artifacts/phase-6-1-verify/results.json`.\n\n**Review across the standard five dimensions** (correctness, readability, architecture, security, performance). Specifically check:\n\n1. **Acceptance-criteria conformance** — does each Phase 6.1 acceptance bullet in `docs/PHASES.md:205-236` have a corresponding test or DOM element? Quote the criterion line and the file:line that satisfies it. Flag any unsatisfied.\n\n2. **Schema integrity** — `db.ts` version(4): is the .stores() declaration verbatim what the decision memo locked in (`sessions: 'id, startedAt', reps: 'id, sessionId, cueId, clipId', settings: 'id', profiles: 'id, createdAt', clips: 'id, importedAt'`)? Are all five tables declared? Does the v3→v4 upgrade test seed a v3 row and reopen at v4?\n\n3. **AddClipResult discriminated union correctness** — does `addClip` exhaustively cover the four declared `reason` values (`quota`, `too-large`, `unsupported-type`, `storage-error`)? Does each have a unit test? Is the QuotaExceededError detection (`isQuotaError`) robust to both DOMException and plain-object error shapes?\n\n4. **DRY / coupling** — `ClipLibraryScreen` includes a local `extractDurationMs` helper. Could a future phase (6.2 tag screen, 6.3 runner) need the same? Should it live in `clipmode/library.ts` or a new `clipmode/metadata.ts`? Flag as nit if duplication is foreseeable.\n\n5. **React effect rules** — `ClipLibraryScreen` has two effect-like blocks (the `refresh` useCallback and the inline `useEffect`). Is the duplication justified, or is there a cleaner pattern? Note the `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule that forced the split.\n\n6. **Error handling completeness** — what happens if `URL.createObjectURL` fails in `extractDurationMs`? What if the user picks 10 files at once and the 5th hits a quota error? Does the UI surface the partial-import state?\n\n7. **Security** — file-input accepts `video/mp4,video/quicktime`. Is there any path where uncontrolled HTML or JS could be injected via clip name? (Names are rendered as text content, not innerHTML, but worth double-checking.) Are blob URLs revoked correctly in `extractDurationMs` and in the screen lifecycle?\n\n8. **Bundle / performance** — is the clip-library code lazy-loaded (`React.lazy`) or eagerly bundled into the main chunk? Compare to PairScreen which is lazy. Phase 6.1 bundle delta is +1.79 KB gzip (under the +5 KB budget) — but eager loading is the wrong call if the screen is rarely visited.\n\n9. **Test quality** — for each test in library.test.ts and db.test.ts, would the test fail if the corresponding behavior were reverted? Flag any that wouldn't.\n\n10. **Verify-script gate strictness** — `verify-phase6-1.mjs` C3 (quota text) is marked `best_effort: true`. Is that the right classification? If chromium always exposes `navigator.storage.estimate`, it should be a gate check, not best-effort.\n\n**Output:** return findings categorized as Blockers / Should-Fix / Nits. For each, quote the file:line and explain the issue concretely. Be ruthless about correctness and DRY; relaxed about cosmetics. End with a one-line verdict: APPROVE / REQUEST-CHANGES."}
