[tool_use] Write {"file_path":"/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor/artifacts/phase-approval.json","content":"{\n  \"phase\": \"phase-6.1\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"summary\": \"Phase 6.1: clip library — import, store, list, delete. Persists local .mp4 Blobs in Dexie at `version(4)` alongside an import / list / delete UI accessible from IdleScreen via a 'Manage clips' link. The v4 schema declares all five tables verbatim per decision-memo §'Concern 2' (`sessions: 'id, startedAt'`, `reps: 'id, sessionId, cueId, clipId'`, `settings: 'id'`, `profiles: 'id, createdAt'`, `clips: 'id, importedAt'`); pre-v4 reps remain readable and `where('clipId').equals(...)` on them returns empty (covered by `db.test.ts` v3→v4 upgrade test that seeds a v3 row, reopens at v4, and asserts the row survives). The new `clipId` index lights up in 6.3 when `RepRecord` gains the field. New module `app/src/clipmode/types.ts` defines `ClipRecord` (Blob-bearing) + `AddClipResult` discriminated union (`{ ok: true; clip } | { ok: false; reason: 'quota' | 'too-large' | 'unsupported-type' | 'storage-error'; message }`) + `CLIP_HARD_CAP_BYTES = 200 MB` + `CLIP_SOFT_WARN_BYTES = 100 MB` + `SUPPORTED_CLIP_MIME_TYPES = ['video/mp4']`. New module `app/src/clipmode/library.ts` implements `addClip(file, { durationMs })`, `listClips()`, `deleteClip(id)`, `getQuotaEstimate()`, `quotaBanner(estimate)`, and `isSoftWarnSize(bytes)` — all four AddClipResult.reason branches have unit tests including a stubbed `QuotaExceededError` and a 250 MB blob, exactly per memo §'Concern 4'. New module `app/src/clipmode/metadata.ts` extracts duration via an offscreen `<video>` element (tolerates URL.createObjectURL throws and timeouts by resolving 0) — lives in clipmode/ so 6.2's tag screen and 6.3's runner can reuse it (per code-reviewer S2). New lazy-loaded `app/src/ui/ClipLibraryScreen.tsx` (chunk: 5.36 KB / 2.21 KB gzip) renders the empty-state hint, file input (`accept='video/mp4'`), quota usage text, per-clip rows with name/duration/size and a 'needs tag' marker for untagged clips, delete-with-confirm, warn-banner at >80%, cap-banner at >95%, and a soft-warn banner for >100 MB single clips. IdleScreen gains a `data-testid='manage-clips-link'` button when `onOpenPair`-style `onOpenClips` prop is wired. App.tsx routes `view='clips'` through a `<Suspense>` boundary matching the PairScreen idiom. Verify-script `app/verify-phase6-1.mjs` runs C1–C4 gate-grade checks (Manage clips link present, library screen opens with empty state + close button + import label, quota-text DOM element renders, Close returns to IdleScreen). All four PASS with 0 console errors. M1–M7 manual checklist enumerates real-device QA per QUALITY_GATES.md §B5 (real <video> duration extraction + live navigator.storage math + .mp4-only acceptance + 200 MB cap + 100 MB soft warn). 23 new vitest tests (213 total, was 190; +2 db v3→v4 upgrade, +21 library across addClip/listClips/deleteClip/getQuotaEstimate/quotaBanner/isSoftWarnSize). Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Main bundle 346.49 KB / 107.15 KB gzip (Phase 2b.4 baseline 345.86 / 107.01 — delta +0.63 KB raw / +0.14 KB gzip thanks to lazy-loading; clip-library chunk separated). CSS chunk grew +1.06 KB raw / +0.21 KB gzip for `.clip-library*` styles. Budget was +5 KB gzip total → well under. Code-reviewer (`code-reviewer` agent) returned APPROVE with 0 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits; all five should-fixes applied before this approval (S1 lazy-load via React.lazy matching PairScreen pattern; S2 metadata extraction moved to `clipmode/metadata.ts`; S3 plain-object branch in `isQuotaError` removed since DOMException-only is what's tested + required; S4 URL.createObjectURL wrapped in try/catch returning 0 on throw; S5 verify-script C3 promoted from best-effort to gate check since headless chromium uniformly ships navigator.storage.estimate). Three of four nits applied: N1 dropped 'video/quicktime' to align with PHASES.md mp4-only criterion; N2 wired aria-disabled on the import label so the dead CSS rule now matches; N3 `fetchLibraryState()` helper deduplicates the effect/refresh data-fetch. Nit N4 (use a shared `rngId` helper) skipped — grepped and no such helper exists; `mintClipId` matches the existing pattern in `session.ts:81` and `profiles.ts:18` (each module mints its own `${prefix}-${Date.now()}-${rand}` id). docs/PHASES.md + docs/QUALITY_GATES.md were already updated in the prior Phase-6-decomposition iteration; this iteration touched only code + tests + verify script + results.\",\n  \"decision_memo\": \"artifacts/decision-memo.md\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"New Dexie schema version(4) declares all five tables exactly: sessions, reps (with clipId index), settings, profiles, clips\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/store/db.ts:32-40` declares `this.version(4).stores({ sessions: 'id, startedAt', reps: 'id, sessionId, cueId, clipId', settings: 'id', profiles: 'id, createdAt', clips: 'id, importedAt' })` — verbatim match with decision-memo §'Concern 2' lock-in. `db.test.ts:158-186` 'opens an empty v4 clips table on a fresh database' asserts `db.clips.count() === 0` and would fail if the table were dropped.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"v3 reps remain readable after the v4 upgrade with no data migration; where('clipId').equals(<any>) on a pre-v4 rep returns empty\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`db.test.ts:92-156` 'preserves v3 reps after opening at v4 with the new clips table' seeds a v3 rep via raw Dexie at v3, closes, reopens with v4 schema, asserts the row reads back unchanged AND that `where('clipId').equals('any-clip-id').toArray()` returns `[]`. Would fail if v4's `.stores()` dropped the reps table or broke the upgrade chain.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"addClip(blob) returns a typed AddClipResult discriminated union with the four declared reason branches; per-clip hard cap 200 MB; soft warn at 100 MB\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`clipmode/types.ts:21-30` declares the union. `clipmode/library.ts:29-84` implements it. All four reason branches have unit tests in `library.test.ts`: 'rejects an unsupported MIME type' (line 58), 'rejects a 250 MB blob with reason: too-large' (69), 'returns reason: quota when Dexie throws QuotaExceededError' (80), 'returns reason: storage-error for a generic Dexie failure' (95). 200 MB hard cap = `CLIP_HARD_CAP_BYTES` in types.ts:33; 100 MB soft warn = `CLIP_SOFT_WARN_BYTES` in types.ts:35; `isSoftWarnSize` has boundary + above-soft + above-hard tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"ClipLibraryScreen accessible from IdleScreen via a 'Manage clips' link; lists clips with name, duration, size; supports file import and delete-with-confirm\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx:113-122` renders the `data-testid='manage-clips-link'` button. `App.tsx:48-54` routes `view='clips'` through Suspense → lazy `ClipLibraryScreen`. The screen renders clip rows with name (`.clip-name`) + duration (`formatDuration`) + size (`formatBytes`). Delete fires `window.confirm` before `deleteClip` (line 113). Verify-phase6-1.mjs C1 PASS asserts the link is present; C2 PASS asserts empty-state + close button + import label render. Manual M1–M3 cover real <video> duration extraction + reload persistence + delete behavior per §B5.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"navigator.storage.estimate() surface visible; warning banner at >80%, hard-cap banner at >95%; both branches unit-tested\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`clipmode/library.ts:108-129` defines `getQuotaEstimate()` + `quotaBanner()`. ClipLibraryScreen.tsx:153-170 renders `data-testid='clip-quota-cap'` at >95% and `data-testid='clip-quota-warn'` at >80%. Verify-script C3 PASS (gate-grade) asserts the quota DOM element renders. `library.test.ts:232-249` tests `quotaBanner()` returning 'cap' / 'warn' / 'none' / null — all four bands. `library.test.ts:196-228` tests `getQuotaEstimate()` for API-absent + math + zero-quota + reject branches.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"docs/QUALITY_GATES.md §'Browser-API limitations' is updated to add a Phase-6 entry alongside Phase 2b\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"Already shipped in the prior Phase-6-decomposition iteration; the section header is now '### Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b + Phase 6)' and lists HTML5 <video>, requestVideoFrameCallback, navigator.storage.estimate as the Phase-6 jsdom-untestable surface. Confirmed unchanged this iteration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Lint + tsc + vitest + vite build clean. Bundle growth budget: +5 KB gzip\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"All four are clean. 213/213 vitest tests pass. Bundle: main 346.49 KB / 107.15 KB gzip (Phase 2b.4 baseline 345.86 / 107.01); delta +0.63 KB raw / +0.14 KB gzip. CSS chunk +1.06 KB raw / +0.21 KB gzip. Lazy-loaded ClipLibraryScreen chunk: 5.36 KB / 2.21 KB gzip. Total user-visible delta well under +5 KB gzip budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Manual real-device QA documented at app/verify-phase6-1.mjs + artifacts/phase-6-1-verify/results.json\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"verify-phase6-1.mjs writes M1–M7 manual_qa_checklist to results.json: M1 (import small/medium/large clip), M2 (reload persists), M3 (delete with confirm), M4 (>200 MB rejected), M5 (non-mp4 rejected), M6 (quota math reflects sum of clip sizes), M7 (>100 MB shows soft-warn banner). Automated run: C1 PASS + C2 PASS + C3 PASS + C4 PASS, console_errors=0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manual_qa\": {\n    \"device_used\": \"not_performed_by_agent\",\n    \"performed_by\": \"autonomous-agent\",\n    \"performed_at\": \"2026-05-27\",\n    \"playwright_run\": {\n      \"automated_gate_checks\": \"C1, C2, C3, C4 PASS — IdleScreen renders the Manage clips link; clicking it opens ClipLibraryScreen with empty-state hint + import label + close button visible; the navigator.storage.estimate DOM element renders (gate-grade per code-reviewer S5 since headless chromium uniformly ships the API); Close returns to IdleScreen with Start drill visible. Zero console errors across all four contexts.\",\n      \"console_errors\": 0\n    },\n    \"checklist_pending_operator_sign_off\": [\n      \"M1 — Import a ~5 MB, ~50 MB, and ~150 MB .mp4 file. All three appear with non-zero duration.\",\n      \"M2 — Reload the page; all three clips persist with the same metadata.\",\n      \"M3 — Delete one clip via the Delete button; the confirm prompt fires; the clip disappears and reload does not show it.\",\n      \"M4 — A >200 MB .mp4 import is rejected with the '200 MB cap' error banner.\",\n      \"M5 — A non-mp4 file import is rejected with the 'type not supported' error banner.\",\n      \"M6 — After importing several clips, the quota banner text reflects navigator.storage.estimate within a few MB of the sum of clip sizes.\",\n      \"M7 — A >100 MB clip import shows the soft-warning banner (data-testid='clip-soft-warn').\"\n    ],\n    \"operator_sign_off_instructions\": \"Update artifacts/phase-6-1-verify/results.json — set each entry's `signed_off` to {date: 'YYYY-MM-DD', device: '<laptop OS + browser version>'} after exercising the step on a real laptop with a real .mp4 file. The §B5 concession requires this field to be populated before the phase is considered fully closed for real-world use; the autonomous loop cannot perform real-video + real-Dexie-blob QA. M1+M2+M3 prove the import / persist / delete primary loop; M4+M5 prove the failure-mode UX; M6+M7 prove the quota and soft-warn signals.\"\n  },\n  \"gates\": {\n    \"testing\": \"213/213 vitest tests pass (Phase 2b.4 baseline 190; +23 new). Every new public behavior in clipmode/library.ts has a would-fail-if-reverted test: addClip happy path + four reason branches + negative-duration clamp; listClips ordering + empty; deleteClip success + missing-id no-op; getQuotaEstimate four edge cases; quotaBanner four bands; isSoftWarnSize three boundary points. Dexie v4 schema has would-fail tests for the v3→v4 upgrade and the fresh-v4 clips table. The lazy-loaded UI surface (ClipLibraryScreen) is gated by verify-phase6-1.mjs C1–C4 — same pattern as Phase 2b's UI flows per the §B5 concession.\",\n    \"dry\": \"clipmode/library.ts is the single source for clip storage operations. clipmode/metadata.ts is the single source for duration extraction — moved out of ClipLibraryScreen.tsx per code-reviewer S2 so 6.2's tag screen and 6.3's runner can reuse it. clipmode/types.ts holds the AddClipResult union + size constants + supported MIME types — consumed by the library, screen, and (later) the runner. No duplication between the screen's data-fetch effect and its refresh handler — both call a shared `fetchLibraryState()` helper (code-reviewer N3).\",\n    \"drift\": \"No prior-phase invariants touched. SessionRecord, RepRecord, ProfileRecord, SettingsRecord schemas unchanged. Existing Dexie v3 records (sessions/reps/settings/profiles) read back unchanged after v4 upgrade (covered by db.test.ts). The new `clipId` index on `reps` is declared but `RepRecord` does not gain the field until 6.3 — pre-6.3 reps simply do not appear in `where('clipId').equals(...)` queries, which is the intended behavior per the decomposition memo. PairScreen / TrainerScreen / SettingsScreen / IdleScreen all continue to work; IdleScreen gained one optional prop `onOpenClips?` which existing callers can omit safely.\",\n    \"planning\": \"Phase 6 was decomposed in the prior iteration via strategy-planner + architecture-red-team round-trip, recorded in artifacts/decision-memo.md `## Phase 6 decomposition memo` + `### Red-team review` + `### Resolved red-team blockers`. Phase 6.1 acceptance criteria in docs/PHASES.md were the locked-in source of truth for this iteration; no new planner invocation needed. Architecture-red-team not re-invoked — no new architectural surface (the storage strategy, the typed-result discriminated union, and the §B5 manual-QA gate were all settled in the decomposition memo).\",\n    \"verification_sprint\": \"Pre-phase: 190/190 vitest tests + lint + tsc + vite build at the Phase 2b.4 boundary all clean (re-confirmed at the top of this iteration). Post-phase: 213/213 + lint + tsc + build all clean. Verify-phase6-1.mjs C1–C4 PASS, 0 console errors.\",\n    \"pre_commit_verify\": \"scripts/phasekit-verify.sh runs lint + typecheck + tests; all pass.\"\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"architecture_red_team\": \"Cross-cutting Phase-6 concerns (§B5 browser-API limitations + §B6 falsifiable acceptance) unchanged in this phase — both were locked in during the prior decomposition iteration and are observed here (manual_qa block + every acceptance criterion is AUTO+GATE or MANUAL with explicit rationale). No new architectural risks introduced.\",\n    \"code_reviewer\": \"APPROVE with 0 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits. All five should-fix items APPLIED before approval: (S1) ClipLibraryScreen lazy-loaded via React.lazy matching the PairScreen idiom — main bundle delta went from +5.71 KB raw to +0.63 KB raw, screen now ships as its own 5.36/2.21-KB chunk; (S2) `extractDurationMs` moved from ClipLibraryScreen.tsx to a new `clipmode/metadata.ts` for reuse by 6.2/6.3 per the §B5 placement guidance; (S3) `isQuotaError` plain-object branch removed since `instanceof DOMException` is what the test covers and what the memo's Concern 4 requires; (S4) `URL.createObjectURL` wrapped in try/catch in extractDurationMs so a synchronous throw resolves the duration as 0 instead of propagating an unhandled rejection; (S5) verify-script C3 promoted from `best_effort: true` to a gate check since headless chromium uniformly ships `navigator.storage.estimate` — `gateChecks = ['C1', 'C2', 'C3', 'C4']` now. Three of four nits APPLIED: (N1) dropped `video/quicktime` from `SUPPORTED_CLIP_MIME_TYPES` and the `accept` attribute to match PHASES.md's mp4-only criterion; (N2) wired `aria-disabled={busy || banner === 'cap'}` onto the import label so the existing CSS rule matches; (N3) `fetchLibraryState()` shared helper deduplicates the effect/refresh data-fetch paths. Nit N4 (shared `rngId` helper) skipped after verifying no such helper exists in the codebase — `mintClipId` matches the established `${prefix}-${Date.now()}-${rand}` pattern in `session.ts:81` and `profiles.ts:18`.\",\n    \"qa_playwright\": \"Phase 6.1 user-visible surface is gated by automated checks C1–C4 in verify-phase6-1.mjs (all PASS) plus the M1–M7 manual checklist under §B5. Real `<video>` duration extraction and real-quota math cannot be exercised under headless chromium; manual operator sign-off is the authoritative gate for those paths per the decision memo §B5 concession. Phase 5 + Phase 2b regression: not separately re-run this iteration; covered by the full vitest suite (213/213) which gates the analytics + drill + profiles + WebRTC pairing + motion + InputSource modules unchanged in this phase.\"\n  },\n  \"suggested_commit_message\": \"phase-6.1: clip library — Dexie v4 + addClip typed result + lazy ClipLibraryScreen\"\n}\n"}
